new information on a high-stakes mystery  we've been covering for years now the  c.i.a says that most cases of the  neurological illness known as havana  syndrome remember that were not were not  caused by a foreign adversary senior  investigative correspondent catherine  herridge has the latest on all this  catherine i think this was surprising  news for a lot of people good morning  tony it was for many good morning the  cia has released new interim findings  overnight on hundreds of reported cases  of havana syndrome ultimately ruling out  russia cuba or any other foreign group  as the cause of most of these illnesses  instead the majority of reports can be  reasonably explained by medical  conditions or environmental and  technical factors including previously  undiagnosed illnesses after a cluster of  cases was first reported in cuba u.s  diplomats and personnel stationed  overseas said they experienced havana  syndrome symptoms including in china  austria and vietnam some told cbs news  they heard ringing or loud piercing  sounds and felt intense pressure in the  face with pain nausea and dizziness a  recent study conducted for the state  department found the most plausible  cause was directed pulsed radio  frequency energy the cia said about two  dozen priority cases remain unexplained  and the focus of active investigation  russian and cuban officials have  consistently denied involvement gail  all right catherine thank you very much
 

